<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Chord ships unsandboxed. It is distributed direct/notarized (Developer ID),
	     not through the Mac App Store, which requires sandboxing — and an
	     unsandboxed browser can spawn native-messaging hosts (third-party
	     integrations) and write anywhere, neither of which the sandbox permits.
	     This is the same trade Chrome/Firefox/Edge make.

	     Without the sandbox the keys that used to live here become moot:
	       network.client, files.user-selected.read-write,
	       files.downloads.read-write, print, device.camera,
	       device.microphone, device.audio-input
	     Camera/mic/print/downloads still work via TCC (the usage strings in
	     Info.plist); no entitlements are needed.

	     On-disk data moves from the sandbox container to the real
	     ~/Library/Application Support — see AppEnvironment.live(), which migrates
	     it on first launch. -->
</dict>
</plist>